same source Z at beta. The beta actor kernel is central elementary; both
actor-kernel images retain their literal intersections and original map.

The literal six-path root now has exactly the five interior source cores
as its covering image. With the source opposite-transporter equations, this
is the original four-core residual and supplies G_i^(2)=R_j^+ Z_i, with
j=i-3, and disjointness. The same decomposition is applied to the original
alpha actor kernel. Constructing these transporter equations on every path
of the chosen apartment, identifying that kernel with Z_i, its natural action
and the compatible reversing reflection remain required by DGS (14.9)(c),
pp.215--216. Both original endpoint maps, the full Borel and the earlier
source scope are preserved by re-export.
